      "text": "================================================================================\n🌐 HTML5 COMPLETE REVISION MASTER NOTES\n================================================================================\n\n🟦 MODULE 1: TEXT STRUCTURE & SEMANTIC TYPOGRAPHY\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n1. HEADING TAGS (<h1> to <h6>)\n   Importance Hierarchy: <h1> (Highest) ──> <h6> (Lowest)\n\n   • <h1> Main / Most Important Heading\n   • <h2> Level 2 Heading\n   • <h3> Level 3 Heading\n   • <h4> Level 4 Heading\n   • <h5> Level 5 Heading\n   • <h6> Smallest Heading\n\n2. PARAGRAPH TAG\n   • <p> : Used to write standard text paragraphs.\n\n3. TEXT FORMATTING & SEMANTIC MARKS\n   • <strong>  ► Semantic importance (Browsers render as bold)\n   • <b>       ► Visual bold formatting only\n   • <em>      ► Semantic emphasis (Browsers render as italic)\n   • <i>       ► Visual italic styling only\n   • <u>       ► Underlined text\n   • <ins>     ► Inserted text (Rendered with underline)\n   • <del>     ► Deleted text (Rendered with strikethrough)\n   • <sub>     ► Subscript / Below baseline (e.g., H₂O)\n   • <sup>     ► Superscript / Above baseline (e.g., X²)\n   • <mark>    ► Highlighted text\n\n4. VOID / UNPAIRED TAGS\n   • <br> ► Line Break (Forces text to next line)\n   • <hr> ► Horizontal Rule (Creates a thematic divider line)\n\n💡 SEMANTIC VS VISUAL:\n   - <strong> / <em> tell browsers/screen readers the MEANING of content.\n   - <b> / <i> only change visual appearance.\n\n\n🟦 MODULE 2: HTML LIST ARCHITECTURE\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n2.1 ORDERED LIST (<ol>)\n    Used when sequence/order matters. Contains <li> (List Items).\n\n    Code Example:\n    <ol type=\"1\" start=\"5\" reversed>\n        <li>HTML</li>\n        <li>CSS</li>\n        <li>JavaScript</li>\n    </ol>\n\n    Attributes:\n    • type=\"\"   ► Sets numbering style:\n                  \"1\" (1, 2, 3)   | \"A\" (A, B, C) | \"a\" (a, b, c)\n                  \"I\" (I, II, III)| \"i\" (i, ii, iii)\n    • start=\"\"  ► Sets starting number (e.g., start=\"5\" begins at 5)\n    • reversed  ► Counts backwards (e.g., 3, 2, 1)\n\n    ⚠️ SYNTAX RULE: Separate attributes with SPACES, never commas!\n    ✅ Correct:   <ol type=\"A\" start=\"5\">\n    ❌ Incorrect: <ol, type=\"A\", start=\"5\">\n\n2.2 UNORDERED LIST (<ul>)\n    Used when sequence does NOT matter.\n\n    Code Example:\n    <ul style=\"list-style-type: square;\">\n        <li>Python</li>\n        <li>Java</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    CSS Bullet Types (list-style-type):\n    • disc   ► ● Default filled bullet\n    • circle ► ○ Unfilled circle\n    • square ► ■ Solid square\n    • none   ► Removes bullets\n\n2.3 DESCRIPTION LIST (<dl>)\n    Used for key-value pairs, glossaries, or term descriptions.\n\n    Code Example:\n    <dl>\n        <dt>HTML</dt>\n        <dd>HyperText Markup Language</dd>\n        <dt>CSS</dt>\n        <dd>Cascading Style Sheets</dd>\n    </dl>\n\n    Memory Hook:\n    • DL = Description List (Wrapper)\n    • DT = Description Term (The Name)\n    • DD = Description Details (The Meaning)\n\n\n🟦 MODULE 3: HYPERLINKS & NAVIGATION\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nANCHOR TAG (<a>)\nCreates hyperlinks to external pages, internal sections, or files.\n\n• Basic Link:    <a href=\"https://google.com\">Google</a>\n• File Download: <a href=\"file.pdf\" download>Download PDF</a>\n\nAttributes:\n• href     ► Specifies destination URL/path\n• download ► Prompts browser to download resource instead of opening it\n• target = \"_blank\"\n              \"_parent\"\n              \"_self\" (by default)\n              \"top\"\n• # is used to mention id \n\n<a href=\"#Heading\" target=\"_top\"> Click here </a>\n\n\n🟦 MODULE 4: MULTIMEDIA TAGS\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n4.1 IMAGE TAG (<img>) — [ Void Tag ]\n    <img src=\"photo.jpg\" alt=\"My Photo\" width=\"300\" height=\"200\">\n\n    • src    ► File location path\n    • alt    ► Alternative text for screen readers / broken links\n    • width  ► Image width\n    • height ► Image height\n\n4.2 AUDIO TAG (<audio>)\n    <audio controls autoplay loop muted>\n        <source src=\"song.mp3\" type=\"audio/mpeg\">\n    </audio>\n\n4.3 VIDEO TAG (<video>)\n    <video controls width=\"500\" autoplay loop muted>\n        <source src=\"video.mp4\" type=\"video/mp4\">\n    </video>\n\nControl Attributes Summary:\n• controls ► Displays play, pause, volume, fullscreen UI\n• autoplay ► Starts playback automatically\n• loop     ► Replays continuously\n• muted    ► Starts playback without audio\n\n\n🟦 MODULE 5: TABLE ARCHITECTURE\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nBASIC TABLE STRUCTURE:\n<table>\n    <thead>\n        <tr>\n            <th>Name</th>\n            <th>Age</th>\n        </tr>\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n        <tr>\n            <td>Rahul</td>\n            <td>20</td>\n        </tr>\n    </tbody>\n</table>\n\nMERGING & SPACING:\n• colspan=\"N\" ► Merges cells HORIZONTALLY across N columns\n• rowspan=\"N\" ► Merges cells VERTICALLY across N rows\n\n• CELL PADDING ► Space INSIDE the cell (Between content & border)\n                 CSS: td, th { padding: 10px; }\n\n• CELL SPACING ► Space BETWEEN individual cells\n                 CSS: table { border-spacing: 10px; }\n\n\n🟦 MODULE 6: FORMS & INPUT CONTROLS\n\nLabel tag is used before the input to tell the user what to write in input we can add a label to input fields\nits improve user readability \n\nAnother way to indicate the format inside input is placeholder \n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n🔹 1. TEXT & INPUT TYPES (<input type=\"...\">)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n• type=\"text\"           ► Standard single-line text entry\n• type=\"password\"       ► Masked characters (●●●●●)\n• type=\"email\"          ► Validates email format (requires '@')\n• type=\"number\"         ► Numeric input with increase/decrease steppers\n• type=\"url\"            ► Validates web addresses (http:// or https://)\n• type=\"search\"         ► Search input field (often renders a clear 'X' button)\n\n🔹 2. DATE & TIME PICKERS\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n• type=\"date\"           ► Select Year, Month, and Day (YYYY-MM-DD)\n• type=\"datetime-local\" ► Select Date AND Local Time (no timezone)\n• type=\"week\"           ► Select a specific Week and Year (e.g., Week 12, 2026)\n• type=\"month\"          ► Select Month and Year (e.g., August 2026)\n\n🔹 3. CHOICE & SELECTION INPUTS\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n• type=\"radio\"          ► Select ONE option from a group\n• type=\"checkbox\"       ► Select MULTIPLE options independently\n• type=\"color\"          ► Opens native OS color picker tool\n• type=\"range\"          ► Slider control for choosing values within a range\n\n🔹 4. FILE UPLOADS & SUBMISSION\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n• type=\"file\"           ► File selection button\n  - accept=\".mp3,.pdf\"  ► Restricts allowed file formats\n  - multiple            ► Allows selecting more than one file at once\n• type=\"submit\"         ► Button that submits all form data to the server\n\n🔹 5. OTHER FORM CONTROLS\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n• <select> + <option>   ► Dropdown menu selector\n                          Example: <select><option>car</option></select>\n• <textarea>            ► Multi-line expandable text box (for bio, comments)\n• <button>              ► Clickable button element (Can also submit forms)\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n🏷️ LABEL & INPUT CONNECTION\n\n📌 Core Concept\n• 'for' attribute goes in <label>\n• 'id' attribute goes in <input>\n• Values MUST match exactly\n\n💻 Code Example\n<label for=\"user-email\">Email:</label>\n<input type=\"email\" id=\"user-email\">\n\n⚡ Key Benefits\n• Clickable Text: Clicking label focuses the input\n• Accessibility: Screen readers speak label text\n• Better UX: Crucial for radio & checkbox targets\n\n🧠 Memory Hook\n• <label for=\"X\">  -->  \"Looking for ID = X\"\n• <input id=\"X\">   -->  \"I am ID = X\" \n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n🧠 QUICK MEMORY HOOKS\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n• file accept=\"\"  ► Filters file types\n• file multiple   ► Pick >1 file\n• radio vs check  ► Radio = Pick 1  | Checkbox = Pick Many\n• select / option ► Dropdown list\n• textarea        ► Multi-line text box\n\n\n🟦 MODULE 7: FULL ARCHITECTURE MAP\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n🌐 HTML5 TAG ARCHITECTURE\n│\n├── 🔤 TEXT CONTENT\n│   ├── h1 - h6 (Headings 1 to 6)\n│   ├── p       (Paragraph)\n│   ├── strong  (Semantic Bold)\n│   ├── b       (Visual Bold)\n│   ├── em      (Semantic Italic)\n│   ├── i       (Visual Italic)\n│   ├── u       (Underline)\n│   ├── ins     (Inserted Text)\n│   ├── del     (Deleted / Strikethrough)\n│   ├── sub     (Subscript - H₂O)\n│   ├── sup     (Superscript - X²)\n│   ├── mark    (Highlight)\n│   ├── br      (Line Break)\n│   └── hr      (Horizontal Divider)\n│\n├── 📋 LISTS\n│   ├── ol      (Ordered List)\n│   ├── ul      (Unordered List)\n│   ├── dl      (Description List Wrapper)\n│   ├── dt      (Description Term)\n│   └── dd      (Description Details)\n│\n├── 🔗 LINKS & MULTIMEDIA\n│   ├── a       (Anchor / Hyperlink)\n│   ├── img     (Image)\n│   ├── audio   (Audio Player)\n│   └── video   (Video Player)\n│\n├── 📊 TABLES\n│   ├── table   (Table Wrapper)\n│   ├── thead   (Table Header Group)\n│   ├── tbody   (Table Body Group)\n│   ├── tfoot   (Table Footer Group)\n│   ├── tr      (Table Row)\n│   ├── th      (Header Cell)\n│   ├── td      (Data Cell)\n│   ├── colspan (Merge Horizontal Columns)\n│   └── rowspan (Merge Vertical Rows)\n│\n└── 📝 FORMS & INPUTS\n    ├── form    (Form Wrapper)\n    ├── input   (User Input Field)\n    └── button  (Clickable Action Button)\n\n\n🧠 SUPER-FAST MEMORY CHEAT SHEET\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n• <h1>-<h6>  ► Headings (Highest to Lowest)\n• <p>        ► Paragraph\n• <strong>   ► Semantic Bold\n• <b>        ► Visual Bold\n• <em>       ► Semantic Italic\n• <i>        ► Visual Italic\n• <sub>      ► Subscript (Below -> H₂O)\n• <sup>      ► Superscript (Above -> X²)\n• <ol>       ► Ordered List\n• <ul>       ► Unordered List\n• <dl>       ► Description List\n• <a>        ► Link (Destination = href)\n• <img>      ► Image (Unpaired / Void)\n• <table>    ► Data Table\n• colspan    ► Merge across Columns\n• rowspan    ► Merge across Rows\n• padding    ► Space INSIDE cell\n• spacing    ► Space BETWEEN cells\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "================================================================================\n🌐 HTML5 COMPLETE REVISION MASTER NOTES\n================================================================================\n\n🟦 MODULE 1: TEXT STRUCTURE & SEMANTIC TYPOGRAPHY\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n1. HEADING TAGS (<h1> to <h6>)\n   Importance Hierarchy: <h1> (Highest) ──> <h6> (Lowest)\n\n   • <h1> Main / Most Important Heading\n   • <h2> Level 2 Heading\n   • <h3> Level 3 Heading\n   • <h4> Level 4 Heading\n   • <h5> Level 5 Heading\n   • <h6> Smallest Heading\n\n2. PARAGRAPH TAG\n   • <p> : Used to write standard text paragraphs.\n\n3. TEXT FORMATTING & SEMANTIC MARKS\n   • <strong>  ► Semantic importance (Browsers render as bold)\n   • <b>       ► Visual bold formatting only\n   • <em>      ► Semantic emphasis (Browsers render as italic)\n   • <i>       ► Visual italic styling only\n   • <u>       ► Underlined text\n   • <ins>     ► Inserted text (Rendered with underline)\n   • <del>     ► Deleted text (Rendered with strikethrough)\n   • <sub>     ► Subscript / Below baseline (e.g., H₂O)\n   • <sup>     ► Superscript / Above baseline (e.g., X²)\n   • <mark>    ► Highlighted text\n\n4. VOID / UNPAIRED TAGS\n   • <br> ► Line Break (Forces text to next line)\n   • <hr> ► Horizontal Rule (Creates a thematic divider line)\n\n💡 SEMANTIC VS VISUAL:\n   - <strong> / <em> tell browsers/screen readers the MEANING of content.\n   - <b> / <i> only change visual appearance.\n\n\n🟦 MODULE 2: HTML LIST ARCHITECTURE\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n2.1 ORDERED LIST (<ol>)\n    Used when sequence/order matters. Contains <li> (List Items).\n\n    Code Example:\n    <ol type=\"1\" start=\"5\" reversed>\n        <li>HTML</li>\n        <li>CSS</li>\n        <li>JavaScript</li>\n    </ol>\n\n    Attributes:\n    • type=\"\"   ► Sets numbering style:\n                  \"1\" (1, 2, 3)   | \"A\" (A, B, C) | \"a\" (a, b, c)\n                  \"I\" (I, II, III)| \"i\" (i, ii, iii)\n    • start=\"\"  ► Sets starting number (e.g., start=\"5\" begins at 5)\n    • reversed  ► Counts backwards (e.g., 3, 2, 1)\n\n    ⚠️ SYNTAX RULE: Separate attributes with SPACES, never commas!\n    ✅ Correct:   <ol type=\"A\" start=\"5\">\n    ❌ Incorrect: <ol, type=\"A\", start=\"5\">\n\n2.2 UNORDERED LIST (<ul>)\n    Used when sequence does NOT matter.\n\n    Code Example:\n    <ul style=\"list-style-type: square;\">\n        <li>Python</li>\n        <li>Java</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    CSS Bullet Types (list-style-type):\n    • disc   ► ● Default filled bullet\n    • circle ► ○ Unfilled circle\n    • square ► ■ Solid square\n    • none   ► Removes bullets\n\n2.3 DESCRIPTION LIST (<dl>)\n    Used for key-value pairs, glossaries, or term descriptions.\n\n    Code Example:\n    <dl>\n        <dt>HTML</dt>\n        <dd>HyperText Markup Language</dd>\n        <dt>CSS</dt>\n        <dd>Cascading Style Sheets</dd>\n    </dl>\n\n    Memory Hook:\n    • DL = Description List (Wrapper)\n    • DT = Description Term (The Name)\n    • DD = Description Details (The Meaning)\n\n\n🟦 MODULE 3: HYPERLINKS & NAVIGATION\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nANCHOR TAG (<a>)\nCreates hyperlinks to external pages, internal sections, or files.\n\n• Basic Link:    <a href=\"https://google.com\">Google</a>\n• File Download: <a href=\"file.pdf\" download>Download PDF</a>\n\nAttributes:\n• href     ► Specifies destination URL/path\n• download ► Prompts browser to download resource instead of opening it\n• target = \"_blank\"\n              \"_parent\"\n              \"_self\" (by default)\n              \"top\"\n• # is used to mention id \n\n<a href=\"#Heading\" target=\"_top\"> Click here </a>\n\n\n🟦 MODULE 4: MULTIMEDIA TAGS\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n4.1 IMAGE TAG (<img>) — [ Void Tag ]\n    <img src=\"photo.jpg\" alt=\"My Photo\" width=\"300\" height=\"200\">\n\n    • src    ► File location path\n    • alt    ► Alternative text for screen readers / broken links\n    • width  ► Image width\n    • height ► Image height\n\n4.2 AUDIO TAG (<audio>)\n    <audio controls autoplay loop muted>\n        <source src=\"song.mp3\" type=\"audio/mpeg\">\n    </audio>\n\n4.3 VIDEO TAG (<video>)\n    <video controls width=\"500\" autoplay loop muted>\n        <source src=\"video.mp4\" type=\"video/mp4\">\n    </video>\n\nControl Attributes Summary:\n• controls ► Displays play, pause, volume, fullscreen UI\n• autoplay ► Starts playback automatically\n• loop     ► Replays continuously\n• muted    ► Starts playback without audio\n\n\n🟦 MODULE 5: TABLE ARCHITECTURE\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nBASIC TABLE STRUCTURE:\n<table>\n    <thead>\n        <tr>\n            <th>Name</th>\n            <th>Age</th>\n        </tr>\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n        <tr>\n            <td>Rahul</td>\n            <td>20</td>\n        </tr>\n    </tbody>\n</table>\n\nMERGING & SPACING:\n• colspan=\"N\" ► Merges cells HORIZONTALLY across N columns\n• rowspan=\"N\" ► Merges cells VERTICALLY across N rows\n\n• CELL PADDING ► Space INSIDE the cell (Between content & border)\n                 CSS: td, th { padding: 10px; }\n\n• CELL SPACING ► Space BETWEEN individual cells\n                 CSS: table { border-spacing: 10px; }\n\n\n🟦 MODULE 6: FORMS & INPUT CONTROLS\n\nLabel tag is used before the input to tell the user what to write in input we can add a label to input fields\nits improve user readability \n\nAnother way to indicate the format inside input is placeholder \n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n🔹 1. TEXT & INPUT TYPES (<input type=\"...\">)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n• type=\"text\"           ► Standard single-line text entry\n• type=\"password\"       ► Masked characters (●●●●●)\n• type=\"email\"          ► Validates email format (requires '@')\n• type=\"number\"         ► Numeric input with increase/decrease steppers\n• type=\"url\"            ► Validates web addresses (http:// or https://)\n• type=\"search\"         ► Search input field (often renders a clear 'X' button)\n\n🔹 2. DATE & TIME PICKERS\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n• type=\"date\"           ► Select Year, Month, and Day (YYYY-MM-DD)\n• type=\"datetime-local\" ► Select Date AND Local Time (no timezone)\n• type=\"week\"           ► Select a specific Week and Year (e.g., Week 12, 2026)\n• type=\"month\"          ► Select Month and Year (e.g., August 2026)\n\n🔹 3. CHOICE & SELECTION INPUTS\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n• type=\"radio\"          ► Select ONE option from a group\n• type=\"checkbox\"       ► Select MULTIPLE options independently\n• type=\"color\"          ► Opens native OS color picker tool\n• type=\"range\"          ► Slider control for choosing values within a range\n\n🔹 4. FILE UPLOADS & SUBMISSION\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n• type=\"file\"           ► File selection button\n  - accept=\".mp3,.pdf\"  ► Restricts allowed file formats\n  - multiple            ► Allows selecting more than one file at once\n• type=\"submit\"         ► Button that submits all form data to the server\n\n🔹 5. OTHER FORM CONTROLS\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n• <select> + <option>   ► Dropdown menu selector\n                          Example: <select><option>car</option></select>\n• <textarea>            ► Multi-line expandable text box (for bio, comments)\n• <button>              ► Clickable button element (Can also submit forms)\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n🏷️ LABEL & INPUT CONNECTION\n\n📌 Core Concept\n• 'for' attribute goes in <label>\n• 'id' attribute goes in <input>\n• Values MUST match exactly\n\n💻 Code Example\n<label for=\"user-email\">Email:</label>\n<input type=\"email\" id=\"user-email\">\n\n⚡ Key Benefits\n• Clickable Text: Clicking label focuses the input\n• Accessibility: Screen readers speak label text\n• Better UX: Crucial for radio & checkbox targets\n\n🧠 Memory Hook\n• <label for=\"X\">  -->  \"Looking for ID = X\"\n• <input id=\"X\">   -->  \"I am ID = X\" \n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n🧠 QUICK MEMORY HOOKS\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n• file accept=\"\"  ► Filters file types\n• file multiple   ► Pick >1 file\n• radio vs check  ► Radio = Pick 1  | Checkbox = Pick Many\n• select / option ► Dropdown list\n• textarea        ► Multi-line text box\n\n\n🟦 MODULE 7: FULL ARCHITECTURE MAP\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n🌐 HTML5 TAG ARCHITECTURE\n│\n├── 🔤 TEXT CONTENT\n│   ├── h1 - h6 (Headings 1 to 6)\n│   ├── p       (Paragraph)\n│   ├── strong  (Semantic Bold)\n│   ├── b       (Visual Bold)\n│   ├── em      (Semantic Italic)\n│   ├── i       (Visual Italic)\n│   ├── u       (Underline)\n│   ├── ins     (Inserted Text)\n│   ├── del     (Deleted / Strikethrough)\n│   ├── sub     (Subscript - H₂O)\n│   ├── sup     (Superscript - X²)\n│   ├── mark    (Highlight)\n│   ├── br      (Line Break)\n│   └── hr      (Horizontal Divider)\n│\n├── 📋 LISTS\n│   ├── ol      (Ordered List)\n│   ├── ul      (Unordered List)\n│   ├── dl      (Description List Wrapper)\n│   ├── dt      (Description Term)\n│   └── dd      (Description Details)\n│\n├── 🔗 LINKS & MULTIMEDIA\n│   ├── a       (Anchor / Hyperlink)\n│   ├── img     (Image)\n│   ├── audio   (Audio Player)\n│   └── video   (Video Player)\n│\n├── 📊 TABLES\n│   ├── table   (Table Wrapper)\n│   ├── thead   (Table Header Group)\n│   ├── tbody   (Table Body Group)\n│   ├── tfoot   (Table Footer Group)\n│   ├── tr      (Table Row)\n│   ├── th      (Header Cell)\n│   ├── td      (Data Cell)\n│   ├── colspan (Merge Horizontal Columns)\n│   └── rowspan (Merge Vertical Rows)\n│\n└── 📝 FORMS & INPUTS\n    ├── form    (Form Wrapper)\n    ├── input   (User Input Field)\n    └── button  (Clickable Action Button)\n\n\n🧠 SUPER-FAST MEMORY CHEAT SHEET\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n• <h1>-<h6>  ► Headings (Highest to Lowest)\n• <p>        ► Paragraph\n• <strong>   ► Semantic Bold\n• <b>        ► Visual Bold\n• <em>       ► Semantic Italic\n• <i>        ► Visual Italic\n• <sub>      ► Subscript (Below -> H₂O)\n• <sup>      ► Superscript (Above -> X²)\n• <ol>       ► Ordered List\n• <ul>       ► Unordered List\n• <dl>       ► Description List\n• <a>        ► Link (Destination = href)\n• <img>      ► Image (Unpaired / Void)\n• <table>    ► Data Table\n• colspan    ► Merge across Columns\n• rowspan    ► Merge across Rows\n• padding    ► Space INSIDE cell\n• spacing    ► Space BETWEEN cells\n\n",
